/Title (The largest loan to transfer to special servicing in July was the $280.0 million CALI 2024-SUN loan, which moved to special servicing for imminent balloon/maturity default. The loan reached its scheduled maturity on July 9 and now carries non-performing matured balloon status, with servicer commentary indicating the borrower is unable to meet the conditions for a maturity extension. The collateral is two full-service beachfront hotels in Santa Monica, CA.)
