/Title (New transfers to special servicing totaled roughly $1.69 billion across 41 loans and were unusually concentrated in retail, which accounted for about $903.6 million. The flow was dominated by regional malls reaching their balloon maturities. Loans that cured, were modified and returned, or paid off were far smaller in aggregate, at roughly $326.4 million.)
