/Title (Loans leaving special servicing in July, through returns to the master servicer or payoffs, totaled approximately $326.4 million across six loans, a much lighter month for resolutions than for transfers. The two largest exits were both retail loans that had reached maturity and were worked out rather than liquidated.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 956 0 R
/Next 1002 0 R
>>
endobj
1002 0 obj
<<
/Title (The largest exit was a portion of the Williamsburg Premium Outlets loan. Roughly $99.5 million across two 2016 conduit deals returned to the master servicer in July as part of a corrected mortgage loan resolution that has now returned the full loan, a roughly $183.8 million obligation, split across four 2016 conduit deals, to regular servicing. The loan)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 956 0 R
/Prev 1001 0 R
>>
endobj
1003 0 obj
<<
/Title (transferred in December 2025 for imminent balloon and maturity default, but remained current throughout its time in special servicing, and it was modified to a new maturity of February 2029. The collateral is a 522,133-square-foot outlet center in Williamsburg, VA, built in 1987 and renovated in 2005. For full-year 2025, the loan reported a DSCR \(NCF\) of 2.11x with occupancy of about 80%, roughly in line with 2024.)
